            "review_title": "Review at Hai San 77",
            "review_text": "Mr.H\nNewtown, Pennsylvania132 contributions\n0\nA gem!\nJan 2014 • Friends\nWhile traveling in Vietnam and visiting friends and family I was taken to this little road side eatery. If you are in South East Asia you will see these places EVERYWHERE and they usually look dirty and unfriendly. What is nice about this place is it is on a paved road so there is very little dust. We sat down last night around 7:30pm and it was cool and quiet aside from the scooter traffic. I was pleasantly surprised at the food we ate. We had steamed clams and grilled squid. The clams came out in a ginger and lemon grass broth and was terrific! I will try and attaché photos as soon as possible! The clams came out in a boiling metal dish and tasted so good we had seconds. We also had the grilled squid and that was wonderful as well. The two orders of clams and one of squid was around $15USD plus a few waters. Honestly, if I was not heading back to HCMC I would have stayed longer. The owners are very quiet and pleasant, highly recommended. Be a traveler and enjoy!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten February 2, 2014",
